field — Declares data members on classes and required data members on interfaces.

Syntax:
  interface HasId {
    id: string
  }
  
  class User {
    id string
    display_name: string
    implements HasId {}
  }

Class fields may use `name Type` or `name: Type`. Interface fields use `name: Type` and are satisfied by same-named class fields or by field mappings inside an `implements` block, such as `id as user_id`. A class value is constructed with an object literal like `User { id: "u1", display_name: "Ada" }`; BAML does not use `new` constructors.
